<h2 id="trigger" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">1. Trigger phrase</h2>

When the user says something like:

> **create paragraph practice for** `Describing words` / `adjectives` / `This/that` / `determiners`

…or mentions **`paraprac`** with a knowledge-area name that already has Basic knowledge + Basic practice — implement **all** of:

1. Learner Paragraph practice UI under `/practice/<area>/paragraph` (noun-phrase uses `/practice/noun-agreement/paragraph`).
2. Paragraph admin support in the **single admin owned by the top-level glossary** (Verb / Noun / Other Word): add a **Generate scope**, never one midlevel admin chip per knowledge area.
3. Backend pool + generate + list/delete + grade wired to the same `content_type` / `content_id` (+ optional `field`) as that area’s Basic practice, with `practice_kind=paragraph`.

Do **not** invent a one-off cloze UI or a local-only grader that never hits `record_attempt`.

**Resolve the area** from the label or suite id (`adjectives`, `determiners`, `contractions`, …) via `knowledgeRoute` / suite configs. If Basic practice is missing, stop and say so (point at **basicprac**).

