<h2 id="product" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">2. Product contract</h2>

| Rule | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **2.1 Mirror Basic inputs** | Whatever Basic practice asks the learner to **fill** (textbox) or **select** (toggle/dropdown) is what each paragraph blank asks for — same control family (`PracticeBlankInput` text vs `selectOptions`). For Places article toggles: keep tokens lowercase (`o | a | —`) and only offer plural (`os/as`) on rows where Basic allows plural. |
| **2.2 Shared chrome** | Learner blanks render through `ParagraphBlankExerciseItem` (+ filter bar patterns from noun/conj). Admin uses the same control strip + DataGrid conventions as `GenderNounParagraphAdminPage` / conj paragraph admin (Generate scope, N, Varieties, Dry run, Generate, Delete, LPL telemetry columns). |
| **2.3 Stats identity** | Grade via `record_attempt` with the area’s **canonical** `MODE_CONTENT_TYPE` mode, the same `content_type` + `content_id` as Basic, optional `field` for multi-slot Basics (`fem` / `masc` / `fem_pl` / `masc_pl` / `form`), and **`practice_kind=paragraph`**. Profile can merge or split by kind. |
| **2.4 Generation** | Non-conjugation: **Alt A** via shared `run_natural_paragraph_units` — natural [target_lang] → LLM language verify → local whole-token presence → deterministic inject ([`REFACTOR_GLOSSARY_PARAGRAPH_NATURAL_THEN_INJECT.md`](../../cursor_gen/refactor_plans/completed/REFACTOR_GLOSSARY_PARAGRAPH_NATURAL_THEN_INJECT.md)). Default is **2 LLM calls**. Multi-sense homographs may **opt in** to a 3rd sense-anchor call — see [§2.6](#sense-anchor). Shared spine for Noun gender + Other Word admins. Do not ship marker-first glossary produce. |
| **2.5 Admin ownership** | Exactly one paragraph-admin chip/page per top-level glossary. Under Other Word Glossary, adjectives / determiners / contractions become Generate scopes on `/admin/other-words/paragraph`. |

Conjugation remains the intensity/PLGW specialty; glossary areas follow the **noun gender** paragraph shape (scope + lemma/item checklist + Varieties), not the verb×tense batch picker — unless the area is conjugations.

<h3 id="sense-anchor" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">2.6 Sense-anchor (opt-in 3rd LLM call)</h3>

#### Why it exists

Default Alt A punches blanks **left-to-right by surface string**. That works when each blank’s spelling is unique in the paragraph. It **fails** when several blanks share the **same spelling** but different **meanings** (homographs): LTR inject can attach the wrong occurrence to the wrong sense. Sense-anchor adds a separate LLM step that tags each listed meaning (`token⦃slot⦄`) before local inject — so blanks bind by **sense**, not by first match.

#### When to use it (agent guideline)

| Prefer | Guideline |
|--------|-----------|
| **Default OFF** (2-call Alt A) | Ordinary form / agreement drills — unique surfaces or “same lemma, one sense per exercise” (adjectives, demonstratives, blending contractions, noun leading/spell/plural, …). |
| **ON** | Same **surface** appears as **more than one pedagogical meaning** in one paragraph (or across blanks that must not be confused), so word-order inject would mis-bind. Canonical example: Para v.s. Por (`para` / `por` senses). |

Keep the guideline **coarse**: if you are unsure, **stay OFF** and say so. Do **not** turn sense-anchor on “just in case” or for cost/quality experiments without a multi-sense bind problem.

#### User prompt vs agent default

1. If the user **explicitly** asks for sense-anchor on or off → **follow that** (do not second-guess).
2. If the user is **silent** → apply the guideline above (**prefer OFF** unless the area clearly looks multi-sense / same-surface-different-meaning).

#### Agent must disclose (new area create / wire only)

When **creating or wiring** a new paragraph area (not when merely regenerating pool rows for an already-wired area), the agent must state the choice **twice** in chat:

1. **At the start** (before implementing / generating): planned mode.
2. **At done** (closeout): what actually shipped.

Use a short, greppable line each time, for example:

```text
Sense-anchor: OFF (default 2-call Alt A) — <one-line why>
```

or

```text
Sense-anchor: ON (3rd LLM meaning-tag step) — <one-line why>
```

#### Runtime logging (every generated paragraph)

Generation code must emit a **lay-term**, **distinctly colored** log line for **each** Alt A paragraph unit stating whether it was built **with** or **without** sense-anchor (see `tag_paragraph_sense_anchor_mode` in `app/llm_traffic/logging_llm.py`, called from `natural_paragraph_loop`). Do not rely on silent adapter flags alone.

#### How to enable (implementation)

1. Thin prompt adapter (pattern: `PorParaNaturalPromptAdapter`) with **`needs_sense_anchors = True`**, plus `build_sense_anchor_prompt` / `parse_sense_anchor_output`.
2. Select that adapter on the area’s generate path (glossary: `generate_glossary_form_paragraph` by scope).
3. Pass `sense_anchor_max_retries` into `run_natural_paragraph_units` (safe always — **ignored** unless opted in). Budget: YAML `glossary_paragraph.sense_anchor_max_retries` or env `GLOSSARY_PARAGRAPH_SENSE_ANCHOR_MAX_RETRIES`.

**Behavior when ON:** produce → language-verify → sense-anchor → local inject; tag failures retry **only** the sense-anchor call ([`REFACTOR_SENSE_ANCHOR_RETRY_ISOLATED.md`](../../cursor_gen/refactor_plans/completed/REFACTOR_SENSE_ANCHOR_RETRY_ISOLATED.md)). Plans: [`REFACTOR_ALT_A_OPTIONAL_SENSE_ANCHOR.md`](../../cursor_gen/refactor_plans/completed/REFACTOR_ALT_A_OPTIONAL_SENSE_ANCHOR.md).

**Reference:** Para v.s. Por — [§10.5](#examples).

<h3 id="host-leading" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">2.6b Host-leading inject (opt-in local search)</h3>

#### Why it exists

Default Alt A LTR-punches the **graded surface**. That fails when the graded token is a **common article** (`o` / `a`) but the pedagogical host is a **place name**: punching random `a` tokens leaves place names out of the prose (or brackets that do not match the sentence).

#### When to use it

| Prefer | Guideline |
|--------|-----------|
| **ON** | Places article scopes (Continents / Countries / States / Cities / Home & shops): blank = article, host = place. |
| **OFF** | Unique form surfaces (This/that, adjectives, gentílicos, numbers) — surface inject is enough. |
| **Not this** | Multi-sense homographs → use [sense-anchor](#sense-anchor) instead (extra LLM call). |

Host-leading stays **2 LLM calls** plus local gates (unfused prep+article ban → produce
repair; inject blanks bare article **or** fused contraction before host). Flag:
`adapter.needs_host_leading_inject`. Mutually exclusive with sense-anchor.
Plans: [`REFACTOR_PLACE_ARTICLE_HOST_LEADING_INJECT.md`](../../cursor_gen/refactor_plans/completed/REFACTOR_PLACE_ARTICLE_HOST_LEADING_INJECT.md) ·
[`REFACTOR_PLACE_HOST_LEADING_CONTRACTIONS.md`](../../cursor_gen/refactor_plans/completed/REFACTOR_PLACE_HOST_LEADING_CONTRACTIONS.md).

#### Agent disclosure (new area)

```text
Host-leading: ON — Places article blanks punch article before place host
```

or

```text
Host-leading: OFF — graded surface is unique enough for LTR inject
```

#### Runtime logging

Cyan `[PARAGRAPH-HOST-LEADING] WITH|WITHOUT …` via `tag_paragraph_host_leading_mode`.

<h3 id="meaning-brackets" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">2.7 Meaning brackets (per-area cue map)</h3>

Learner paragraph blanks show a trailing **`[…]`** cue (`ParagraphBlankExerciseItem` `meaningBracket`). That string is **not** free-form knowledge prose — it must come from the area’s **Basic practice** column contract ([**basicprac**](basicprac-basic-practice-from-knowledge.mdc) §3):

| Term | Role for brackets |
|------|-------------------|
| **`user_input_cols`** | What the learner **fills** in Basic (and in each paragraph blank). **Never** use these as the bracket cue. |
| **`other_shown_cols`** | Read-only cue columns on Basic practice (Number, Word, Rank, Meaning of Fused, …). Bracket text is chosen **only** from this set. |

**Regulation (all non-conjugation paragraph areas):**

1. **Pool / blank JSON** must set the UI bracket field (`meaning_en` and/or `cue` — whatever the learner mapper reads into `meaningBracket`) from a **per-area cue map** keyed by scope (or `blank_kind` when one scope has multiple blank kinds).
2. **Eligible sources** = values of columns that appear on that area’s **Basic practice** screen as `other_shown_cols` — **not** Basic-knowledge-only columns (Note, Grouping Note, Example, …) unless Basic practice explicitly shows them.
3. **Cardinality:**
   - **Exactly one** eligible `other_shown_col` → that column’s value **is** the bracket (auto).
   - **More than one** → human or agent picks the **most suitable** primary cue for that drill and records it in the cue map (and in the area’s worked example in [§10](#examples)). Prefer: identity cue (Number / Word / Rank / Place) when the blank is a form/article fill; prefer **Meaning / sense** when Basic shows it and the blank is multi-sense (e.g. Para v.s. Por) or sense-anchor is ON.
4. **Implement** the choice in code (registry / pool builder / blank assembler) — do not leave “whatever gloss the pool had” as the default.

**Examples:** Cardinals Basic = Form (input) + Number (shown) → brackets = **Number** (e.g. `1.000`), not knowledge Note. Para v.s. Por Basic = Word (input) + Meaning (shown) → brackets = **Meaning**. Place article Basic = Article (input) + Place (shown) → brackets = **Place**.

